{"id":"extsuite-dot-separator-boundary","kind":"matcher","pattern":"dir/@(*)","path":"dir/.b","flags":["extglob"],"expected":false,"oracle_expected":true,"source":"zlob_1_6_3","disputed":true,"note":"Ferralk preserves the documented hidden-component boundary; zlob 1.6.3's public matcher consumes the leading dot inside this extglob."}
{"id":"extsuite-star-run-before-zero-or-more","kind":"matcher","pattern":"**(a)","path":"x","flags":["extglob","match_hidden"],"expected":true,"oracle_expected":false,"source":"zlob_1_6_3","disputed":true,"note":"Bash and ksh give the final star in a run to the `*(` extglob opener; zlob 1.6.3 greedily collapses the whole run before looking for a group. Issue #305."}
{"id":"extsuite-embedded-star-run-before-zero-or-more","kind":"matcher","pattern":"a**(b)","path":"a","flags":["extglob","match_hidden"],"expected":true,"oracle_expected":false,"source":"zlob_1_6_3","disputed":true,"note":"The outer star and the zero-or-more group can both consume nothing. Ferralk follows the shell grammar rather than zlob's inherited tokenization. Issue #305."}
{"id":"extsuite-long-star-run-before-zero-or-more","kind":"matcher","pattern":"***(a)","path":"x","flags":["extglob","match_hidden"],"expected":true,"oracle_expected":false,"source":"zlob_1_6_3","disputed":true,"note":"All but the final star remain an ordinary wildcard run; the last star opens the group, matching Bash and ksh. Issue #305."}
{"id":"extsuite-escaped-star-before-group","kind":"matcher","pattern":"\\x5C*@(a)","path":"*a","flags":["extglob"],"expected":true,"source":"handwritten","note":"An escaped star before a group is the literal star. Bash 5.2 with extglob agrees."}
{"id":"extsuite-escaped-star-before-group-rejects-backslash","kind":"matcher","pattern":"\\x5C*@(a)","path":"\\x5Cxa","flags":["extglob"],"expected":false,"source":"handwritten","note":"An escape has only its escaped reading: a literal backslash followed by the star read as a wildcard is not a second branch. Bash 5.2 and zlob matchExtglob consume the escape and reject the candidate."}
{"id":"extsuite-escaped-star-after-group","kind":"matcher","pattern":"*(a)\\x5C*","path":"aa*","flags":["extglob"],"expected":true,"source":"handwritten","note":"An escaped star after a repeated group is the literal star. Bash 5.2 with extglob agrees."}
{"id":"extsuite-escaped-star-after-group-rejects-backslash","kind":"matcher","pattern":"*(a)\\x5C*","path":"\\x5Cx)\\x5C","flags":["extglob"],"expected":false,"source":"handwritten","note":"The zero-width group and the escape cannot be re-read as a literal backslash, a wildcard and a trailing literal backslash. Bash 5.2 rejects the candidate."}
{"id":"extsuite-escaped-star-behind-outer-star-rejects-backslash","kind":"matcher","pattern":"*\\x5C*@(a)","path":"x\\x5Cxa","flags":["extglob"],"expected":false,"source":"handwritten","note":"The retained interpreter with an outer star gives the escape the same single reading as the positive NFA. Bash 5.2 rejects the candidate."}
